# Health checks for the published services on GRANDPA - one URL per line, `#`
# comments stripped before use. Checked on 127.0.0.1 rather than the tailscale
# IP on purpose: these answer "is the app answering", and a tailscale blip must
# not page several times at once - the published path itself is `tailscaled`,
# which a systemd unit sv-watch already watches.
#
# Copied from scripts/thinkcentre/http-endpoints 2026-10-22 and RE-WRITTEN for
# this box, because the copy would have been a lie: every line over there names
# a ThinkCentre container (immich, paperless, vaultwarden, stirling-pdf,
# syncthing, searxng, caddy) that does not exist here, and a sweep that checks
# eight dead URLs reports eight failures every 60 s. That is the exact drift
# the count-comment in the old file exists to prevent, so the list was rebuilt
# from what THIS host actually runs rather than filtered from theirs.
#
# Any HTTP status counts as UP (302, 303 and 401 are healthy here - half these
# services redirect to a login). Only `000`, meaning nothing answered at all,
# is a failure. Two consecutive strikes are required before a page, so a cold
# boot with containers still starting never alerts.
#
# LAST VERIFIED 2026-10-22.
